explanation:
Per 45 CFR §164.512(j), A covered entity may, consistent with applicable law and standards of ethical conduct, use or disclose PHI, if the covered entity, in good faith, believes the use or dislosure is (1) necessary to prevent or lesson a serious and imminent threat to the health or safety of a person or the public and; (2) is to a person or persons reasonably able to prevent or lessen the threat, including target of threat. Per 45 CFR §164.512(f)(2), The covered entity may disclose only the following information:

(A) Name and address;

(B) Date and place of birth;

(C) Social security number;

(D) ABO blood type and rh factor;

(E) Type of injury;

(F) Date and time of treatment;

(G) Date and time of death, if applicable; and

(H) A description of distinguishing physical characteristics, including height, weight, gender, race, hair and eye color, presence or absence of facial hair (beard or moustache), scars, and tattoos.
